&lt;h2&gt;Which prompts should I track to reflect real buyer intent?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;According to &lt;a href="https://www.responsive.io/resources/whitepapers/inside-the-b2b-buyers-mind-2025"&gt;Responsive research&lt;/a&gt;, 56% of tech buyers are turning to generative AI to build vendor shortlists. Answer engines increasingly drive which brands buyers consider before they ever visit a website.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Tracking prompts shows marketers whether their brand appears where buyers are asking, how it’s described, and which competitors and sources are winning those answers instead.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;How do branded, unbranded, and competitor prompts work?&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Think about prompts in three broad categories: branded, unbranded, and competitor.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h4&gt;Branded Prompts&lt;/h4&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Branded prompts include the company or product name, such as “What is [Brand]?” or “Does [Brand] integrate with Salesforce?”&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Important note: In the same way that a brand will rank for its branded keyword in traditional SEO, answer engines should always mention the brand here, so presence isn’t the metric. Branded prompts protect brand accuracy in AI answers. For branded prompts, the focus is sentiment and accuracy.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h4&gt;Unbranded Prompts&lt;/h4&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Unbranded prompts describe a problem or category without naming any company, such as “best project management software for agencies” or “how to reduce client onboarding time.” Unbranded solution-seeking prompts measure discovery-stage visibility. Unbranded prompts usually reveal the biggest gaps and should make up the largest share of a prompt set.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;In my experience, unbranded prompts deserve the same priority as unbranded keywords in traditional SEO. Search teams often judge search performance by branded demand, but search teams and stakeholders must understand that nonbranded search plays a critical role in performance as well.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Increasing brand visibility is mostly the job of PR, brand marketing, and wider visibility efforts. Search supports that work, but a search team’s core role is to reach buyers who are still discovering their options and don’t yet know which brands to consider. In AI search, unbranded prompts are where that discovery happens. Unbranded prompts are the clearest measure of whether answer engine optimization (AEO) is reaching new buyers, tying visibility as directly as possible to a search team’s efforts.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h4&gt;Competitor Prompts&lt;/h4&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Competitor prompts reveal where rivals appear during evaluation. Competitor prompts name one or more rivals, such as “Is [Competitor] good for remote teams?” or “alternatives to [Competitor].” Answers to these prompts show which brands answer engines consider as the category’s default options, and whether the brand appears as a credible alternative.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Pro Tip: If possible, track prompts for three to five direct competitors. Keep the focus on competitors who have solid marketing strategies and perform well online.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Ideally, marketers will track prompts that fall under all three categories of branded, unbranded, and competitor.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Using dedicated tools for prompt tracking, instead of manual checks, makes spotting trends more manageable for marketers. &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot’s AEO tool&lt;/a&gt; gives marketers one place to monitor prompts and track brand visibility across ChatGPT, Gemini, and Perplexity. Teams can compare how often competitors appear on the same prompts, review which sources answer engines cite, and turn findings into clear, prioritized recommendations.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For Marketing Hub Professional and Enterprise customers, AEO is included and uses CRM data to suggest prompts to track, rather than relying on generic industry templates. HubSpot’s AEO tool is also available standalone for $50/month (25 prompts included).&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/screenshot%20shows%20the%20HubSpot%20prompt%20dashboard%20where%20prompts%20are%20tracked.%20The%20dashboard%20includes%20example%20prompts%20and%20visibility%20percentages..webp?width=650&amp;amp;height=332&amp;amp;name=screenshot%20shows%20the%20HubSpot%20prompt%20dashboard%20where%20prompts%20are%20tracked.%20The%20dashb...

&lt;p&gt;Marketers choosing between Ahrefs Brand Radar and Profound are really asking whether AI visibility belongs in&amp;nbsp;your SEO suite or in a dedicated AEO platform. Brand Radar is the first option, Profound is the second, and &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt; is a third worth testing if you want visibility data connected to content and marketing workflows.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Brand Radar is enough for most Ahrefs-first teams. Profound earns its price when you need specialist depth, and HubSpot AEO fits teams that want tracking and next steps in one place. Below, we compare all three on engines, prompts, citations, sentiment, and price.&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
