&lt;h2&gt;Ahrefs Brand Radar vs. Profound Summary and Verdict&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Here’s the verdict before the detail.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brand Radar&lt;/strong&gt; fits SEO-native teams. It sits inside Ahrefs, so AI visibility data lives next to keywords, backlinks, rank tracking, and site audits.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profound&lt;/strong&gt; fits teams that want depth. It adds consumer-panel prompt volumes, ChatGPT Shopping analytics, server-log crawler tracking, and no-code agents, but its public pricing now points to a demo-led Enterprise sale.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; fits marketers who want visibility data to turn into prioritized recommendations and, with Marketing Hub Pro or Enterprise, content and campaign action inside the same platform.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The connected case is simple. Tracking tells you where you’re missing, and recommendations tell you what to publish. HubSpot AEO covers both — start free below.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What Each Tool Measures&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A few terms make the comparison easier to read.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AEO (answer engine optimization)&lt;/strong&gt; is the practice of improving how your brand appears in AI-generated answers.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Answer engines&lt;/strong&gt; are tools like ChatGPT, Gemini, and Perplexity that respond with a direct answer instead of a list of links.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prompts&lt;/strong&gt; are the questions people ask those engines.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentions&lt;/strong&gt; are times an answer names your brand.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Citations&lt;/strong&gt; are times it links to your pages as a source.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AI visibility tools measure brand presence, mentions, citations, sentiment, and competitive share in answer engines. Traditional rank trackers can’t fully measure brand presence in AI-generated answers, because there’s no fixed position to track. That gap matters. A 2025 &lt;a href="https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2025/07/22/google-users-are-less-likely-to-click-on-links-when-an-ai-summary-appears-in-the-results/"&gt;Pew Research Center analysis&lt;/a&gt; of 900 U.S. adults’ browsing found users clicked a traditional result link in 8% of visits that showed a Google AI summary, versus 15% of visits without one. When fewer people click, being named inside the answer carries more weight.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The three tools come from different places. Ahrefs Brand Radar is an AI visibility feature associated with the Ahrefs SEO workflow. Profound is a dedicated AEO and AI intelligence platform. HubSpot AEO is a visibility tracker with recommendations, and it connects to the HubSpot platform. If you’re still mapping the landscape, our guide to &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/ai-search-engines"&gt;AI search engines&lt;/a&gt; covers how each engine sources its answers.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Ahrefs Brand Radar Strengths and Limitations&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/brand%20radar.webp?width=650&amp;amp;height=500&amp;amp;name=brand%20radar.webp" width="650" height="500" alt="ahrefs brand radar dashboard" style="height: auto; max-width: 100%; width: 650px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block;"&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Brand Radar’s biggest draw is its data source. Ahrefs builds its prompt database from real keywords, expands them into natural questions using People Also Ask and semantic fanout, then runs them through each AI platform. Ahrefs’ &lt;a href="https://help.ahrefs.com/en/articles/11064852-what-is-brand-radar-and-how-to-use-it"&gt;help center&lt;/a&gt; cites more than 405 million search-backed prompts, and its &lt;a href="https://ahrefs.com/brand-radar"&gt;product page&lt;/a&gt; cites 448 million or more. The figure has moved between first-party pages, so check the live number before you quote it.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengths&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SEO crossover.&lt;/strong&gt; Brand Radar connects to Site Explorer, Keywords Explorer, Rank Tracker, Site Audit, and Bot Analytics. If your team already lives in Ahrefs, you won’t add a login.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engine breadth.&lt;/strong&gt; The prompt index covers AI Overviews, AI Mode, ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, and Copilot. Custom prompts add Claude. Grok appears in Ahrefs’ help documentation, though new data collection there is temporarily paused.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Off-site sources.&lt;/strong&gt; Brand Radar tracks YouTube, Reddit, and TikTok visibility, which are free while in beta.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instant start.&lt;/strong&gt; You can search any brand in the index without setup. Index responses go back to 2025.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting options.&lt;/strong&gt; Ahrefs offers Repor...

&lt;p&gt;Large language model (LLM) visibility tools track brand mentions, citations, and share of voice across answer engines. &lt;a href="https://digitaloft.co.uk/insights/ai-in-seo-statistics"&gt;According to Digitaloft&lt;/a&gt;, 80% of users rely on zero-click results at least 40% of the time, meaning they often get what they need directly from a search engine results page (SERP) or an AI-generated answer. That behavior can leave marketers with fewer on-site signals such as clicks, scroll depth, and engagement rate.&lt;/p&gt;  
&lt;p&gt;LLM visibility tools fill the measurement gap created by zero-click AI results by showing how often and how favorably a brand appears in AI-generated answers. Search engine optimization (SEO) metrics such as clicks, conversions, and keyword position still matter. Answer engine optimization (AEO) adds another layer of measurement by tracking repeated prompts, citations, sentiment, and competitor visibility across answer engines.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;This roundup compares eight LLM visibility tools, from free diagnostics to enterprise platforms, so that marketers can evaluate the right fit for ongoing tracking.&lt;/p&gt; 
